    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS, all tests green).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system.\n\n**`Owner.java`** (`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`):\n- Added `getMembershipPoints()` \u2014 the single-responsibility scorer: starts at 0, `+2` for a present email, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` for a household of 3+ (`householdSize >= 3`), `+3` for tenure over 365 days.\n- Rewrote `getMembershipLevel()` to purely map points \u2192 level: `1` for 0\u20131, `2` for 2\u20133, `3` for 4\u20135, `4` for 6+. It delegates to `getMembershipPoints()` rather than duplicating the factor logic, so each piece of logic lives in one place.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** (the DTO source):\n- Added a `membershipPoints` read-only field so the new value flows through the generated `OwnerDto` (MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n- Updated the `membershipLevel` schema description and raised its `maximum` from 3 to 4 to match the new mapping.\n\nThe existing `OwnerAuditLogger` continues to work since `getMembershipLevel()` is preserved. The new acceptance test (`membershipPoints=3`, `membershipLevel=2` for a fresh owner with email and no namesakes) passes, along with the rest of the suite.",
