    "probe_recall": 0.4634146341463415,
    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (implementing the generated `OwnersApi`). The request body binds to the generated **`OwnerFieldsDto`**, not the `Owner` entity.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Framework Bean Validation (`@Valid @RequestBody`)\n\nRuns before the method body. On failure \u2192 **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`).\n\n- `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`\n- `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`\n- `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n- `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n- `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n- `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)` (optional)\n- `postcode` \u2014 **no** bean constraint (validated imperatively later)\n- `registrationDate` / `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` only; `sharesHousehold` \u2014 none (defaults `false`)\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Imperative validators & normalizers (controller body, in this exact order)\n\n1. **`addressNormalizer.normalize(address)`** \u2014 *side-effect*: trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST\u2192STREET / RD\u2192ROAD / AVE\u2192AVENUE; mutates the DTO's address. (Runs before the required-field check, so that check sees the normalized value.)\n2. **`ownerRequestValidator.validate`** \u2014 required-fields check on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone (`hasText`) \u2192 `RequiredFieldsMissingException` **400**.\n3. **`postcodeValidator.validate`** \u2014 if postcode present: must be 4 digits and within the region range for the city \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` **400**.\n4. **`cityOwnerLimitValidator.validate`** \u2014 DB count; `>= 50` owners in that city \u2192 `CityOwnerLimitExceededException` **409**.\n5. **`registrationDateValidator.validate`** \u2014 supplied date after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` **400**.\n6. **`dailyOwnerLimitValidator.validate`** \u2014 rolls date to a business day; `>= 100` owners registered that day \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` **429**.\n7. **`telephoneNormalizer.normalize(telephone)`** \u2014 *side-effect*: normalizes to E.164 (default country `+61`, strips formatting, drops one leading `0`); requires 8\u201315 digits / valid national length; else `InvalidTelephoneException` **400**. Mutates the DTO telephone.\n8. **`emailNormalizer.normalize(email)`** \u2014 *side-effect*: null/blank \u2192 `null`; else must match email regex (`InvalidEmailException` **400**), returns trimmed + lower-cased. Mutates the DTO email.\n9. **`disposableEmailDomainValidator.validate(email)`** \u2014 blocks mailinator.com / tempmail.com / guerrillamail.com \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` **400**.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Mapping & derived-field side-effects (all before save)\n\n10. **`ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)`** \u2014 builds the `Owner` entity (ignores `id` and `pets`).\n11. **`householdIdGenerator.generate(lastName, postcode)`** \u2192 sets `householdId` (first 12 hex of SHA-256 of the household key).\n12. **Duplicate handling**, branching on `sharesHousehold`:\n    - If `true`: sets `possibleDuplicate = false`, `possibleDuplicateOf = null` (no duplicate check).\n    - If `false`: **`duplicateOwnerValidator.validate`** \u2014 loads all owners, hard-fails on same household key (lastName+postcode) \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` **409**; then **`possibleDuplicateDetector.findPossibleDuplicate`** (soft, never throws) \u2192 sets `possibleDuplicate` flag + `possibleDuplicateOf` id.\n13. **`customerCodeGenerator.generate(postcode, telephone, lastName)`** \u2192 sets `customerCode` (`<REGION>-<HASH8>`).\n14. **`clinicService.countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)`** \u2192 sets `namesakeCount`.\n15. **`householdSizeCalculator.size(owner)`** \u2192 sets `householdSize` (counts same-household owners + 1).\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Persistence\n\n16. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` \u2192 JPA `persist`, which triggers the entity's **`@PrePersist resolveRegistrationDate()`**: if `registrationDate` is null, defaults it to `LocalDate.now()`, then adjusts it forward to a business day (`BusinessDay.onOrAfter`). Hibernate also validates the entity's own `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` constraints (including telephone `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`) on flush.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Post-save side-effects & response\n\n17. **`ownerAuditLogger.created(owner)`** \u2014 SLF4J log to the `\"AUDIT\"` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n18. **Response DTO** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`, plus **`bulkSignupWarningEvaluator.isBulkSignupInEffect()`** set on the DTO (true when > 80 owners registered today).\n19. Sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, returns **201 CREATED**.\n\n---\n\nTwo ordering nuances worth flagging:\n\n- **Normalizers mutate the request DTO in place** before downstream validators run \u2014 e.g. address normalization happens before the required-field check, and telephone/email normalization happens before their respective format/domain validators.\n- **`registrationDate` is finalized only at `@PrePersist` (step 16)**, *after* the registration-date and daily-limit validators (steps 5\u20136) and after all derived fields are computed. So any field derived from the registration date before save can diverge from the value actually persisted when the client omits the date or supplies a weekend/holiday date.\n\nI read the code only; nothing was changed."
